      "title": "跨越青年創生限制：中介組織協作熟齡者參與地方創生之機制初探",
      "title_en": "Beyond Youth-Centric Revitalization: A Preliminary Study on Intermediary Organizations Collaborating with Older Adults in Rural Local Revitalization",
      "abstract": "臺灣地方創生政策偏重青年移居或返鄉，然而在長壽社會的宏觀設計下，如何打破年齡限制，賦能健康中高齡族群成為偏鄉永續發展的生力軍，並豐富其「第三人生」，乃為本研究之核心。本研究採取個案研究法，透過深度訪談與參與觀察，探討雙和醫院與中介組織跨界合作之「平溪森林療癒社會處方計畫」，期能翻轉以青年為中心的地方創生框架，建構熟齡者社會參與與在地連結的新路徑。\n\n該計畫引進預防醫學的社會處方概念，以「在地賦能」為核心，預計培訓 2 至 5 位熟齡居民取得森林療癒師資格；同時，由「臺北醫學大學」、「台灣森林療癒協會」與「台灣觀光地方創生協會」跨界合作，共同擔任「連結者」（Link Workers）角色。這群中介組織扮演資源對接的橋樑，陪伴返鄉創生的熟齡者，將平溪的森林生態、文史、小農餐飲及民宿進行系統性串聯。計畫預計以三年時間，培育熟齡者執行森林療癒綠色處方，並進一步輔導其轉化為兼顧都會區親子與上班族身心紓壓需求的綠色全人健康體驗遊程。\n\n本方案雖處起步階段，但透過首年實踐歷程之觀察，中介組織的陪伴、策略擬定與資源對接，已展現出為熟齡者開創多元第三人生、提升社會參與度的潛力。本研究期能以此跨界合作之實踐歷程，為偏鄉熟齡者的社會參與及社會連結設計，提供具備參考價值的多元觀點與實踐架構。",
      "abstract_en": "Taiwan’s local revitalization policies heavily favor youth migration or return. However, within the macro-design of a longevity society, breaking age constraints to empower healthy older adults as vital forces for rural sustainable development and enriching their \"Third Age\" serve as the core focus of this study. Adopting a case study method, this research utilizes in-depth interviews and participant observation to examine the \"Pingxi Forest Therapy Social Prescribing Project\"—a cross-sector collaboration between Shuang Ho Hospital and multiple intermediary organizations. This study aims to transcend the youth-centric framework of local revitalization and construct a new pathway for older adults’ social participation and local connectedness.\n\nThe project introduces the concept of social prescribing from preventive medicine, prioritizing local empowerment by training two to five older residents to become certified forest therapy guides. Concurrently, Taipei Medical University, the Taiwan Forest Therapy Association, and the Taiwan Sightseeing and Local Revitalization Association cross-sectorally collaborate as \"Link Workers.\" Operating as bridges for resource matching, these intermediaries accompany returned older revitalizers to systematically integrate Pingxi's forest ecology, history, smallholder catering, and homestays. Over a three-year span, the project aims to cultivate older adults to execute green prescriptions and further guide them to transform these into holistic wellness tourism itineraries catering to urban families and office workers.\n\nObservations from the first year demonstrate that intermediary accompaniment, strategic formulation, and resource alignment effectively unlock diverse Third Age plans and enhance engagement. This cross-sector practice provides a multifaceted perspective and an implementation framework for social connection and social participation of older adults in rural areas.",
      "keywords": "第三人生、地方創生、森林療癒、社會處方、高齡者社會參與、連結者",
      "keywords_en": "Local Revitalization, Forest Therapy, Social Prescribing, Link Workers, Third Age, Senior Social Connection,",
      "display_presenters": "蔡文宜",
      "author_info_lines": [
        "蔡文宜 助理教授｜臺北醫學大學醫療暨生物科技法律研究所"
      ],
