      "title": "機構安寧療護中的三方決策：中國內地、香港與台灣的機構住民、家屬及醫療專業人員觀點 之質性統合分析",
      "title_en": "Triadic Decision-Making in Institutional Palliative Care: A Meta-Synthesis of Resident, Family, and Professional Perspectives in the Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong, and Taiwan",
      "abstract": "摘要內文 法規與社會文化脈絡深刻地形塑了中國大陸、香港及台灣的生命終期與安寧療護發展。儘管 中國內地的臨終照護基礎設施仍處於探索階段，台灣已開創性地針對預立醫療照護計畫進行 立法，而香港則持續推廣非立法形式的預設醫療指示。在文化價值的驅動下，不同權益關係 者之間的安寧緩和醫療決策展現出錯綜複雜的互動動態。本研究旨在整合這三個地區中，機 構住民、家屬與醫護人員此三方於生命終期照護中的互動動態。本研究於 2026 年 5 月對\n\nScopus、PubMed、Web of Science、CINAHL Ultimate 及 ProQuest 資料庫進行系統性文獻 回顧，共檢索出 659 篇文獻。納入標準為：近十年內發表、於中國內地、香港及台灣進行 之質性研究，且探討醫護人員、家屬與機構住民於安寧緩和醫療決策過程中的態度、觀點、 張力與互動關係。經摘要篩選與全文審查後，最終納入 14 篇符合所有標準的研究進行深度\n\n分析。本研究採用 Thomas 與 Harden（2008）提出的主題統合分析法，歸納出三大核心主 題：「儒家家庭主義與道德義務」、「保護性隱瞞」以及「多層次脫節」。基於上述主題，本研 究建構了一個反映華人社會安寧緩和醫療決策過程中，三方權益關係者相互影響之動態關係 的「三元概念模型」。此質性統合分析為醫護人員在因應複雜的生命終期決策過程時提供寶 貴見解，並有助於反思其在特定文化脈絡下的系統性盲點。此外，研究結果可作為政策制定\n\n者與機構設計公眾死亡教育之指引，以降低安寧療護決策過程中的衝突與情緒困擾。",
      "abstract_en": "Legislative and socio-cultural landscapes fundamentally shape end-of-life (EOL) and palliative care in the Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong, and Taiwan. While the EOL infrastructure on the Chinese\n\nMainland remains exploratory, Taiwan has pioneering legislation in Advance Care Planning (ACP), and Hong Kong is promoting non-legislative advance directives. Driven by cultural values, the\n\npalliative care decision-making among different stakeholders manifests with intricate dynamics. This research aims to synthesise the EOL care dynamics in the triad of residents in institutionalised care\n\nsettings, families, and healthcare providers conducted in these three regions. A systematic review yielded 659 records from Scopus, PubMed, Web of Science, CINAHL Ultimate and ProQuest in May\n\n2026. The inclusion criteria were: qualitative studies, conducted in the Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong, and Taiwan, published within the recent decade, that explored the tensions and interactions between\n\nhealthcare providers, families, and residents in institutional care settings on their attitudes and perspectives on the palliative care decision-making process. After abstract screening and full-text\n\nreview, 14 studies that met all criteria were identified and reviewed in depth. A thematic synthesis, proposed by Thomas and Harden (2008), was performed, resulting in three primary themes:\n\nConfucian familialism and moral obligations, protective concealment, and a multi-layered disconnect.\n\nBased on these themes, a triadic conceptual model of the interrelated dynamics between the three stakeholders in the palliative care decision-making process within Chinese societies was developed.\n\nThis meta-synthesis offers valuable insights to healthcare providers in navigating the complexity of the end-of-life decision-making process and reflecting on their own systemic blind spots within the\n\ncultural context. Moreover, the findings can further guide policymakers and institutions in designing public death education to minimise conflict and emotional distress within the palliative care decision-\n\nmaking process.",
      "keywords": "安寧療護；決策制定；質性統合分析；生命終期照護；預立醫療照護計畫",
      "keywords_en": "Palliative care; Decision Making; Quantitative Meta-synthesis; End-of-life Care; Advance-care planning",
      "display_presenters": "馮卓奇、蘇枳晴",
      "author_info_lines": [
        "蘇枳晴 學生｜香港中文大學文化及宗教研究系",
        "馮卓奇 講師｜香港都會大學伍絜宜人文社會科學院社會科學系"
      ],
      "author_info_lines_en": [
        "So Chi Ching Master's Student｜The Chinese University of Hong Kong",
        "Fung Cheuk Ki Lecturer｜Hong Kong Metropolitan University"
      ]
