      "title": "終身學習社會的推手：非正規成人教育教學者靈性資源與永續勞動福祉",
      "title_en": "The Promoters of a Lifelong Learning Society: Spiritual Resources and Sustainable Labor Well-being of Non-formal Adult Educators",
      "abstract": "研究目的：本研究旨在探討臺灣非正規成人教育場域中，處於非典型勞動體制下的自由講師，如何實踐多向度靈性資源以抵抗職業困境、轉化情緒耗損，進而重構專業主體性與永續勞動福祉。\n\n研究方法：本研究採質性研究取向，透過半結構式訪談六位具備豐富經驗的自由講師，利用主題分析職涯敘事與教學經驗文本。\n\n主要發現：研究發現包含三個核心面向：(1) 個人認同重構：講師透過向內反思與角色「去權威化」，突破體制桎梏，將生存勞動轉譯為平等的生命陪伴志業；(2) 群體與空間共振：順應成人學習特性，講師打破冰冷的契約關係，締結具溫度的雙向互動社群連結，並藉由大自然經驗與場域的空間共振轉化勞動流動的破碎感；(3) 超越宗教的教學使命：講師展現高度文化混融彈性，結合本土民間信仰與超越宗之信念，將世俗教學昇華為「天職」召喚。\n\n結論：靈性資源並非消極的心理調適，而是教學者在不穩定夾縫中，由內而外發起的「主體覺醒歷程」。本研究建議，政策端應將靈性資源教育之涵育納入非正規師資培力體系，為設計終身學習與長壽社會留住具備教學韌性的優質推手。",
      "abstract_en": "This study aims to explore how non-formal adult educators( freelance lecturers )under the atypical labor system in Taiwan's non-formal adult education sector practice multidimensional spiritual resources to resist occupational challenges, transform emotional exhaustion, and thereby reconstruct their professional subjectivity and sustainable labor well-being. Adopting a qualitative research approach, this study conducted semi-structured interviews with six experienced freelance lecturers and utilized thematic analysis to examine their career narratives and teaching experiences.\n\nThe findings reveal three core dimensions: (1) Reconstruction of personal identity: Through inner reflection and role \"de-authoritization,\" lecturers break through institutional constraints, translating survival labor into an egalitarian vocation of life companionship. (2) Community and spatial resonance: Aligning with adult learning characteristics, lecturers dismantle cold contractual relationships to build warm, two-way interactive community connections. They also transform the fragmented feeling of labor mobility through nature experiences and the spatial resonance of the field. (3) Teaching mission beyond religion: Educators demonstrate high cultural hybridization flexibility, integrating local folk beliefs and transcendent faith to elevate secular teaching into a sacred \"calling.\"\n\nThe conclusion indicates that spiritual resources are not passive psychological adjustments, but rather a \"subjective awakening process\" initiated from within by educators caught in the cracks of instability. This study suggests that policymakers should integrate the cultivation of spiritual resource education into the non-formal teacher training system, in order to retain high-quality promoters with teaching resilience for designing a lifelong learning and longevity society.",
      "keywords": "非正規成人教育、自由講師、靈性資源、終身學習社會。",
      "keywords_en": "Non-formal adult education, Freelance lecturers, Spiritual resources, Lifelong learning society",
