      "title": "超高齡社會的系統性創新：以「不老高手」為核心的服務設計與 AI 賦能人才再造模式研究",
      "title_en": "Systemic Innovation in a Super-Aging Society: A Study on Service Design and AI-Empowered Talent Reconstruction Centered on \"Ageless Masters\"",
      "abstract": "隨著台灣進入超高齡社會，高齡者的社會參與已從單純的「延命」轉向「優化生命」的價值再造。本研究旨在透過服務設計建構「第三人生永續生活大學」系統，將高齡者從被動接收者轉化為具生產力的「社會資產」。本研究採方案開發研究法，結合「七階段人生重啟路徑」（含覺察、培力、實踐等階段）與「五大學院」之課程，並導入AI學習指引與數位教練。本方案於2018年至2019年陸續實施兩屆培訓，共以9位高齡學員（培訓時年齡介於65至81歲）為研究對象。研究採用深度訪談與行動觀察進行資料蒐集，並透過質性主題分析，歸納學員由素人蛻變為「不老高手」的觀點轉化歷程與社會參與效益。\n\n研究發現，學員在歷經「由自我轉向需求中心」的實踐後，實現了顯著的觀點轉化。質性分析顯示，透過AI學習指引與數位教練的輔助，學員能有效克服數位焦慮並提升自我效能感。研究建立之「不老高手」認證機制與五大新職能領域（如健康促進指導員、數位生活教練等），成功輔導兩屆學員於社區展現持續性的社會參與。長期追蹤結果亦顯示，此模式能有效縮短退休後的社會真空期，並透過在地化知識轉譯強化社區互助韌性。",
      "abstract_en": "As Taiwan enters a super-aging society, older adults' social participation has shifted from mere life extension to value reconstruction through life optimization. This study aims to construct a \"Third-Life Sustainable Living University\" system through service design, transforming older individuals from passive service recipients into productive \"social assets.\"\n\nEmploying a program development research method, this study integrates a service framework based on the \"Seven-Stage Life Reboot Path\" (comprising stages such as awareness, empowerment, and practice) and the \"Five Major Academies,\" supplemented by AI learning guide maps and digital coaches. The program was implemented across two cohorts between 2018 and 2019, involving 9 senior participants aged 65 to 81 at the time of training. Data were collected using in-depth interviews and participant observation, and analyzed through qualitative thematic analysis to track the participants' perspective transformation and social engagement outcomes as they evolved from ordinary elders into \"Ageless Masters.\"\n\nThe findings indicate that participants experienced significant perspective transformation after undergoing a practical process of shifting from \"self-centeredness to need-centeredness.\" Qualitative analysis shows that with the support of AI learning guides and digital coaches, participants effectively overcame digital anxiety and enhanced their self-efficacy. The established \"Ageless Master\" certification mechanism and five new occupational domains (such as health promotion instructors and digital life coaches) successfully guided both cohorts to maintain continuous community involvement. Furthermore, long-term tracking results reveal that this model effectively shortens post-retirement social vacuums and strengthens community resilience through localized knowledge translation.",
      "keywords": "第三人生、服務設計、AI 賦能、觀點轉化、不老高手",
      "keywords_en": "Third Life, Service Design, AI Empowerment, Transformative Learning, Ageless Masters",
      "display_presenters": "吳茹慧",
      "author_info_lines": [
        "吳茹慧／中華國際享齡賦能教育發展協會／理事長"
      ],
      "author_info_lines_en": []
