      "title": "照服員作業支持之投影介面設計研究：以日照中心團體活動情境為例",
      "title_en": "Projection Interface Design for Supporting Care Workers: Group Activity Contexts in Adult Day Care Centers",
      "abstract": "台灣已邁入超高齡社會，日照中心團體活動仰賴照服員協調。活動中須兼顧團體引導、安全監測與個別協助，易出現視線資源衝突、雙手被設備佔用與情境判斷中斷。前期需求探索已歸納痛點與設計需求，並建議發展投影式介面，惟尚未轉譯為可檢視的介面設計。為使資訊融入活動場景且抬頭可見，本研究採投影為候選媒介，展開設計轉譯。設計過程參照平靜科技、環境型顯示與免手持互動文獻建立原則，並將投影可視性與環境光線作為概念設計限制，經資訊架構、視覺層級與互動流程規劃，提出三項介面概念；製作介面稿作為實務者檢視刺激物。設計包括：「周邊狀態提示」透過投影畫面邊緣的顏色，顯示全場的參與與安全狀況，目標為讓照服員一眼掌握情況，減少視線移開；「非接觸手勢控制」採空中手勢、確認手勢與游標回饋，降低操作設備造成照護中斷的可能；「分級警示」以位置、色彩與升級行為區分日常提示與安全警告，避免訊息皆以高強度警報呈現。非接觸手勢控制無需持握平板或遙控器。本研究將上述抽象需求轉化為可討論、修正與評估的介面設計物，並由具日照團體活動經驗之實務者進行形成性概念檢視，蒐集其理解方式、使用條件、潛在風險與修正需求，作為後續原型開發與智慧照護服務設計參考。",
      "abstract_en": "Taiwan has become a super-aged society, and group activities in adult day care centers rely heavily on care workers' on-site coordination. During activities, care workers must balance group guidance, safety monitoring, and individual assistance, creating three work-related challenges: conflicting visual attention, hands occupied by devices, and interrupted situational judgment. A prior needs exploration identified these challenges and corresponding design requirements and recommended developing a projection-based interface, yet the requirements remained untranslated into reviewable interface designs. To integrate information into the activity scene and make it visible at a glance, this study adopts projection as a candidate medium for design translation. Literature on calm technology, ambient displays, and touch-free interaction informed the design principles. Projection visibility and ambient lighting served as conceptual design constraints. Information architecture, visual hierarchy, and interaction-flow planning produce three interface concepts; interface mockups serve as stimuli for practitioner review. Three interface designs are proposed. The Peripheral Status Display uses colors along the edge of the projected image to show overall participation and safety conditions in the activity area. It is designed to help care workers grasp the situation at a glance and reduce gaze shifts. The Touch-Free Gesture Control adopts mid-air gestures with gesture-based confirmation and cursor feedback, designed to reduce possible care interruptions caused by device handling. The Graded Alert distinguishes routine cues from safety warnings through position, color, and escalation behavior, avoiding uniformly high-intensity alarms. The touch-free gesture mechanism allows control without holding a tablet or remote control. This study transforms abstract field needs into interface artifacts that can be discussed, revised, and evaluated. Practitioners with group-activity experience in adult day care centers will conduct a formative review of the concepts, and their interpretations, usage conditions, potential risks, and suggested revisions will inform subsequent prototype development and smart-care service design.",
      "keywords": "照顧服務員、日間照顧中心、投影介面、互動設計、智慧照護",
      "keywords_en": "care workers; adult day care centers; projection interface; interaction design; smart care",
      "display_presenters": "余莉苹",
      "author_info_lines": [
        "余莉苹｜中原大學商業設計學系｜碩士生",
        "黃文宗｜中原大學商業設計學系｜副教授"
      ],
      "author_info_lines_en": []
