      "source_files": [
        "J3黃雪芳摘要中文.docx",
        "J3黃雪芳摘要英文.docx"
      ],
      "title": "高齡日照中心AI體感遊戲服務創新模式：探討健康老化、失能預防與社會參與之實踐",
      "title_en": "Innovative AI Exergame Service Models in Senior Daycare Centers: A Study on Healthy Aging, Disability Prevention, and Social Participation",
      "abstract": "研究背景\n\n超高齡社會面臨長照需求激增與照顧人力不足之挑戰，日間照顧中心極需導入創新服務。傳統高齡運動受限於趣味性不足與數據追蹤困難，而新興的AI科技體感遊戲具備即時回饋、遊戲化互動與健康管理優勢，為日照中心提供「失能預防」與「復能」創新路徑。\n\n研究目的\n\n本研究旨在探討AI科技體感遊戲導入日照中心之創新服務模式，評估對高齡者健康老化、失能預防（認知功能與功能性體適能）及促進社會參與、緩解孤獨感之成效，為高齡福祉與科技照護創新提供實證。\n\n研究方法\n\n採準實驗設計，招募日照中心22位高齡者，進行三個月AI體感遊戲與團體運動介入。以認知功能、功能性體適能與孤獨感量表為評估工具，運用無母數統計分析前後測組內與組間變化。\n\n研究發現\n\n歷經三個月介入，高齡者在認知功能與功能性體適能數據皆呈現顯著進步，證實AI體感遊戲能減緩失能。此外，體感遊戲降低高齡者孤獨感，並提升在日照中心的社交互動與參與感。\n\n研究結論\n\n將AI體感遊戲融入日照中心課程，是一項具健康支持與預防失能的創新服務，能透過科技互動重塑高齡者社會連結，體現「活躍老化」精神，作為智慧長照與福祉政策推動之範例。",
      "abstract_en": "Background As super-aged societies face the dual challenges of surging long-term care demands and caregiver shortages, senior daycare centers urgently need to introduce innovative services. Traditional senior exercise programs are often limited by a lack of engagement and difficulties in data tracking. In contrast, emerging AI-powered exergames offer advantages such as real-time feedback, gamified interaction, and health management, providing an innovative path for disability prevention and rehabilitation in daycare centers.\n\nPurpose\n\nThis study aims to explore the innovative service model of integrating AI exergames into senior daycare centers. It evaluates their effectiveness on healthy aging, disability prevention (specifically cognitive function and functional fitness), social participation enhancement, and loneliness alleviation among older adults, thereby providing empirical evidence for innovations in elderly welfare and tech-driven care.\n\nMethods\n\nEmploying a quasi-experimental design, this study recruited 22 older adults from a daycare center to participate in a three-month intervention combining AI exergames and group exercises. Cognitive function, functional fitness tests, and loneliness scales were used as evaluation tools. Non-parametric statistical analyses were applied to evaluate intra-group and inter-group variations between pre- and post-tests.\n\nFindings\n\nFollowing the three-month intervention, the older adults demonstrated significant improvements in both cognitive function and functional fitness metrics, confirming that AI exergames can effectively mitigate disability. Furthermore, the exergames reduced loneliness and enhanced social interactions and a sense of participation within the daycare center.\n\nConclusion\n\nIntegrating AI exergames into daycare center curricula constitutes an innovative service that delivers health support and disability prevention. By reshaping the social connections of older adults through technological interaction, this model embodies the core spirit of active aging and serves as an innovative exemplar for the advancement of smart long-term care and elderly welfare policies.",
      "keywords": "AI科技體感遊戲、日照中心、服務創新、失能預防、社會參與",
      "keywords_en": "AI Exergames, Senior Daycare Centers, Service Innovation, Disability Prevention, Social Participation",
      "display_presenters": "黃雪芳",
      "author_info_lines": [
        "黃雪芳 博士生｜國立臺北科技大學技術及職業教育研究所"
      ],
      "author_info_lines_en": []
