      "title": "基於 RFID 與智慧穿戴裝置之弱勢族群外出安全輔助系統設計",
      "title_en": "",
      "abstract": "本研究針對視障者、聽障者、高齡者、行動不便者、認知障礙者及學童等族群，於外出過程中所面臨之定位困難、路口通行風險、資訊取得不足及走失等問題，建構整合式智慧輔助機制，以提升其外出安全性與自主性。\n\n本系統整合智慧穿戴裝置、RFID 導盲磚、路口中控系統及遠端監測平台。使用者配戴具備 RFID、Wi-Fi、語音播報、震動提示與按鈕控制功能之穿戴裝置，當經過導盲磚時，系統可即時辨識所在位置並建立連線，主動提供地標、店家及路況等環境資訊。當使用者接近路口時，可透過按鈕發送過馬路請求，系統於固定等待時間後切換行人號誌，並同步以語音與震動提示使用者開始通行。\n\n與傳統固定秒數號誌不同，本研究利用 RFID 節點持續監測使用者通行狀態，若於預設綠燈時間內尚未抵達對向人行道，系統將自動啟動一次綠燈延長機制，以降低高齡者及行動不便者滯留車道之風險。此外，本系統設計多模態回饋機制，可依不同使用者需求提供語音或震動提示；並透過移動路徑記錄、安全範圍監測及異常事件判斷，於偏離活動範圍、長時間停留或疑似無法完成通行時，即時通知家屬並提供位置資訊。\n\n本研究透過整合定位辨識、智慧路口控制、多模態回饋及遠端安全監測等功能，使交通環境能主動回應不同弱勢族群需求。預期可有效降低路口事故與走失風險，提升弱勢族群獨立外出能力與安全感，同時減輕家屬照護負擔，進一步提升公共空間之友善性與整體交通安全品質。",
      "abstract_en": "With the advent of an aging society and the increasing mobility needs of vulnerable populations, enhancing travel safety and independence in public spaces has become a critical issue in smart city development. Vulnerable groups, including visually impaired individuals, hearing-impaired individuals, older adults, people with mobility limitations, individuals with cognitive impairments, and schoolchildren, often face higher risks in traffic environments due to limited perception, slower reaction times, or reduced decision-making abilities. Existing assistive facilities are typically designed for single purposes and lack integration and real-time interaction capabilities.\n\nThis study proposes the \"Design of an Outdoor Safety Assistance System for Vulnerable Populations Based on RFID and Wearable Devices,\" which integrates wearable devices, RFID-enabled tactile paving, Wi-Fi communication, and intelligent intersection control mechanisms to establish a comprehensive assistive system. The proposed system provides location identification, smart pedestrian crossing assistance, multimodal feedback, and safety monitoring functions. RFID nodes are used to determine users' positions, while real-time communication between wearable devices and intersection control units enables pedestrian crossing requests, adaptive green-light extensions, voice and vibration feedback, route recording, and geofencing-based monitoring.\n\nThe core concept of this study is to transform conventional fixed-time traffic infrastructures into responsive systems through bidirectional integration between public facilities and personal wearable devices. The modular architecture aims to improve travel safety, enhance environmental awareness, reduce the risks of getting lost and traffic accidents, and increase caregiving efficiency for family members and caregivers.\n\nIn conclusion, the proposed system demonstrates practical feasibility using existing technologies and exhibits considerable potential for future applications in intelligent transportation, accessible environments, and smart caregiving services, contributing to the development of more inclusive and user-friendly public spaces.",
      "keywords": "RFID、智慧路口、弱勢族群、智慧穿戴裝置、物聯網",
      "keywords_en": "RFID, Intelligent Intersection, Vulnerable Populations, Wearable Devices, Internet of Things",
      "display_presenters": "莊舒涵",
      "author_info_lines": [
        "莊舒涵¹、林郁璇²、洪志璒³*、蔡忠憲⁴",
        "¹虎尾科技大學資管系／學生",
        "²中原大學商設系產設組／學生",
        "³高雄師範大學軟工系／學生",
        "⁴高英工商資訊科／教師"
      ],
      "author_info_lines_en": []
